; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  $40-$43  the ground.  The line itself is the top row of the tile, so it
;           lands on y=192 exactly, which is where the dino's feet are and
;           where a cactus sits.  Everything under the line is colour 2, the
;           sand; the variants differ only in the specks sitting on it.  The
;           line is always flat, so a dino never has to follow the terrain.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@tile GROUND_A $40
oooooooo
########
########
########
########
########
########
########

@tile GROUND_B $41
oooooooo
########
########
########
########
########
########
########

@tile GROUND_C $42
oooooooo
########
##o#####
########
########
########
########
########

@tile GROUND_D $43
oooooooo
#####o##
########
########
########
########
########
########

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  $44-$45  grit one tile further down, to stop the band under the line
;           looking empty
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@tile GRIT_A $44
########
###o####
########
########
########
########
########
########

@tile GRIT_B $45
########
########
########
######o#
########
########
########
########

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  $46  the body of the ground, which fills every row below the grit.  Solid
;       colour 2, exactly like the backdrop of the four ground tiles and the
;       two grit ones -- the whole band below the line is one flat colour
;       with the line and the specks drawn over it in colour 1.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@tile SOLID_FILL $46
########
########
########
########
########
########
########
########

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  $47-$48  the two sides of a mountain: one tile of a forty-five degree
;           line, and its mirror.  A whole range is drawn from nothing but
;           these, because every slope in it is the same slope, and the two
;           join up exactly corner to corner however many are laid end to
;           end.  They are drawn in colour 2, which no other background tile
;           uses, so the range gets a colour of its own without costing an
;           attribute byte -- and the triangles are left open, like Super
;           Mario Land's, so the sky shows through them and the dino and the
;           cacti simply pass in front.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@tile MTN_LEFT $47
.......#
......#.
.....#..
....#...
...#....
..#.....
.#......
#.......

@tile MTN_RIGHT $48
#.......
.#......
..#.....
...#....
....#...
.....#..
......#.
.......#

